WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.090
Bev had always loved going to the mall.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:07.630
When she was a child, it meant spending quality
time with her mother, taking in the bustling

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:11.780
sights of the stores, the enticing smells
of the food court.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:17.050
When she was on her best behavior, she might
be rewarded with a new toy, a soft pretzel,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.550
or a fistful of quarters to spend at the arcade.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:25.160
When she was a little bit older, first coming
into her independent teenage spirit, the mall

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.519
was a place of refuge, of freedom.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:33.020
Somewhere she could spend time with her friends
away from her family’s prying eyes, trying

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.980
on outfits she’d never be allowed to wear
to school, filling up on free samples, and

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.070
imagining what it might feel like to be grown
up.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:46.910
But as Bev had gotten older, left behind childish
things, the mall had started to die.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:51.350
She knew it wasn't her fault, but it was sad
to watch the source of so many simple joys

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.520
whither away bit by bit.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.829
Stores closed one by one, driven out of business
by the convenience of online shopping.

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:04.430
Slowly but surely, the thriving center of
her suburban youth hollowed out, turning into

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:09.320
a graveyard of commerce left behind in the
endless march toward the future.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:14.159
The colorful signs and advertisements for
coming attractions remained, but there were

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:15.159
no customers.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:18.711
The phantom smell of uneaten Cinnabon lingered
in the air.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:22.060
The lights were on, but no one was home.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.790
And then, the lights went out too.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.320
The city didn't want to deal with the abandoned
mall's upkeep, but they didn't want to go

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.619
to the trouble of tearing it down, either.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:33.991
So, they just left it there.

00:01:33.991 --> 00:01:37.560
There was a running joke in town that the
last security guard to lock up the place had

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:43.070
left the doors wide open and just let nature
get inside and start taking its course.

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:48.060
The mall belonged to the wild plants and animals
again, a strange, artificial enclosure where

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.540
raccoons could scavenge and deer could hide
from hunters and their rifles.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:58.430
Then, of course, the small town had done what
small towns do best: it fired up the rumor

00:01:58.430 --> 00:01:59.430
mill.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.610
Worried parents passed around email forwards
warning about dangerous drifters hiding out

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:08.380
in the empty mall, or gangs conducting violent
initiations there.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:12.860
Teenagers dared each other to go inside before
chickening out and going home, riling each

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.430
other up with promises of ghosts or evil store
mannequins ready to attack.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:22.170
Children at recess or on scout camping trips
gave each other nightmares with stories of

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:27.610
giant monsters hiding in the old building,
waiting for lost kids to wander inside so

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.220
they could gobble them up.

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:34.989
Bev knew none of that was true, it couldn't
be, but she still couldn't shake the curiosity

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:38.660
she felt about the mall that the town had
left behind.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:40.310
What did it look like now?

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:46.190
What had the elements, the time, the influence
of intruders, both curious and destructive,

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:47.810
done to the place?

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:52.660
She had never planned to get into urban exploring,
but then again, she hadn't planned to move

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.120
back to her hometown after flunking out of
law school either.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:01.640
It was strange, being back in such a familiar
place that now looked so different.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:06.330
She could try to adjust, could let her life
fade into a gray routine of diner breakfasts

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:11.099
and drinks at the one bar in town and endless
cups of coffee, or she could find a way to

00:03:11.099 --> 00:03:14.810
lean into the inherent strangeness of being
back home.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.870
When she bumped into Daniel, her best friend
from high school, and he told her all about

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:23.330
his new, slightly illegal hobby, she knew
she had found the answer.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:29.690
He had a crew of fellow Urban Explorers, a
term they preferred to use instead of "trespassers,"

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:34.810
a mix of friends from high school and other
exploring enthusiasts he had met online.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:40.400
Bev was casually interested, but not entirely
sure if the dangerous hobby was for her, until

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.580
Daniel mentioned the mall.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.659
Like Bev, he had continued thinking about
it long after its official closing.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:51.620
He wanted to go inside, to see what had happened
to it over the years, and to see if there

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.090
was a crumb of truth to any of the rumors
about what lurked inside.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.650
Bev didn't take that part seriously, but her
fascination with the old mall was enough to

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:05.069
convince her to join the crew on their expedition
inside.

00:04:05.069 --> 00:04:09.030
Daniel provided her with a list of rules:
Turn off your cellular data once you get there

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:14.340
so the police can't prove you were trespassing,
bring water, bring a flashlight, and wear

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.560
all black.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.350
The group agreed to meet about a mile away
from the old mall, where they would park their

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:23.400
cars, discuss their plans, and head inside.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.330
Bev felt a bit silly, lying to her parents
about where she was going at her age.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.570
But she didn't want them to worry about her.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.650
She told them she was going to meet up with
some friends at a dance club just out of town.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.080
They didn't bother to ask what kind of club
she would wear a black sweater, black pants,

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:41.360
boots, and a black knit hat to.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:43.889
She was happy to leave without any more scrutiny.

00:04:43.889 --> 00:04:48.419
As she drove out toward the abandoned mall,
she gripped the steering wheel with sweaty,

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:49.539
nervous hands.

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:50.870
What was she thinking?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:53.830
What if something went wrong while they were
in there?

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:57.860
The old building could be full of exposed
wiring, and loose beams just waiting to fall

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.710
down and crush someone.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.680
There could be a nest of rabid animals ready
to defend their territory.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:05.350
She tried to shake off the sense of foreboding.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:10.130
Daniel and his crew had done this sort of
thing dozens of times before.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.710
Everything would be fine.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.900
By the time she pulled up to the meeting spot
and parked her car, Bev had managed to calm

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:17.290
herself down.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:21.449
This would be a fun, weird night of poking
around the ruins of her childhood, the remains

00:05:21.449 --> 00:05:25.810
of a long-gone piece of suburban Americana,
and that was all.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.539
Nothing bad would happen.

00:05:27.539 --> 00:05:31.180
She introduced herself to the rest of the
group, a pair of brothers named Mark and Louis

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:35.420
that she recognized from high school and a
young woman named Rachel who didn't look a

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.759
day over 20.

00:05:36.759 --> 00:05:39.470
She must have been one of Daniel's internet
buddies.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.780
"Is this everybody?"

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:41.780
Bev asked.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.780
Daniel nodded.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.259
"This is the crew for tonight.

00:05:44.259 --> 00:05:45.259
Ready?"

00:05:45.259 --> 00:05:46.259
"Ready as I'll ever be."

00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:48.069
Bev shrugged and laughed.

00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:52.020
Everyone else nodded in agreement, holding
up their various flashlights, excited to get

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.639
into the mall and explore.

00:05:53.639 --> 00:05:58.509
The place was every bit as fascinating as
Bev had hoped it would be, a mixture of almost

00:05:58.509 --> 00:06:03.419
untouched storefronts, clothes rotting off
of their eternal plastic mannequins beneath

00:06:03.419 --> 00:06:08.680
plastic signs advertising Going Out of Business
sales, and the wild world encroaching on what

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:12.569
had once been a piece of suburban retail paradise.

00:06:12.569 --> 00:06:17.380
Spiderwebs hung along the walls, possums and
rats skittered along the floors, vines crept

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:22.889
along the remains of the fountain at the center
of the food court that had long ago run dry.

00:06:22.889 --> 00:06:26.960
Bev screamed in shock as something ran across
her foot, but when she cast her flashlight

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.759
beam at it she found that it was just a small
raccoon, running from the sudden intrusion

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:32.910
on its home.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.690
"Sorry, I'll keep my cool next time."

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.060
She laughed it off.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:38.060
"It's fine.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.139
It happens to me too."

00:06:39.139 --> 00:06:40.139
Daniel reassured her.

00:06:40.139 --> 00:06:43.520
"You never quite get used to roaming around
these places in the dark.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.169
But look, there's a lot of cool stuff to check
out."

00:06:45.169 --> 00:06:49.960
He used his flashlight to illuminate the food
court, specifically the soft pretzel stand.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.440
On top of the stand, leaning precariously
to one side, was the enormous model of a soft

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.069
pretzel that had once attracted hungry shoppers
looking for a snack.

00:06:58.069 --> 00:06:59.069
"Hungry?"

00:06:59.069 --> 00:07:00.069
He quipped.

00:07:00.069 --> 00:07:03.349
Bev couldn't help herself, she pulled out
her phone and snapped a picture.

00:07:03.349 --> 00:07:09.720
It was creepy, it was a little sad, but mostly
it was a reminder of the simple joys of childhood.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:13.990
When the flash went off, it illuminated the
darkness behind the stand, and she caught

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:17.820
the glow reflecting in the eyes of the animals
hiding back there.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:22.539
It unsettled her at first, but she reminded
herself, this place was theirs now.

00:07:22.539 --> 00:07:26.129
She and Daniel and everyone else, they were
just visiting for the night.

00:07:26.129 --> 00:07:29.199
She checked her phone to see how the picture
came out, and frowned.

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:30.230
"Hey, Daniel?

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:31.270
Look at this."

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:34.169
She held out her phone to show him, and his
eyes widened.

00:07:34.169 --> 00:07:35.229
"What is that?

00:07:35.229 --> 00:07:36.229
Can you zoom in?"

00:07:36.229 --> 00:07:38.979
Bev zoomed in on the picture, and the two
took a closer look.

00:07:38.979 --> 00:07:43.729
There, in the background of the picture, just
barely illuminated by the phone's flash, was

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.199
a large silhouette.

00:07:45.199 --> 00:07:49.490
They couldn't make out any defining features
other than a large, round head, and long,

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.090
thin, noodle-like arms.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:54.259
"Did this place used to have a mascot, or
something?"

00:07:54.259 --> 00:07:55.259
Daniel asked.

00:07:55.259 --> 00:07:56.310
Bev shook her head.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.960
"Not that I remember."

00:07:57.960 --> 00:07:58.960
"Huh."

00:07:58.960 --> 00:07:59.960
Daniel sighed.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:00.960
"Weird.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:01.960
Anyway.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:02.960
Where'd the others go?"

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.139
He looked around for their flashlights, or
any other sign of life.

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:05.139
"Guys?

00:08:05.139 --> 00:08:06.180
Did you get lost?"

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:10.229
His voice echoed through the wide, empty space,
but no one responded.

00:08:10.229 --> 00:08:11.229
"Hello?!"

00:08:11.229 --> 00:08:14.379
Bev called out, a chill running down her spine.

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:18.349
Only minutes ago, she had heard the others
laughing and joking around as they explored

00:08:18.349 --> 00:08:23.040
the other end of the mall, but now she couldn't
hear a thing.

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.540
Even the chittering of the rats had gone quiet.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:30.919
Suddenly, a bloodcurdling scream rang out,
and sent Bev's heart leaping into her throat.

00:08:30.919 --> 00:08:34.839
She and Daniel shared a look of deep concern
as they both silently wondered if their worst

00:08:34.839 --> 00:08:36.580
fears had come to pass.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:37.700
Had someone fallen?

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.169
Had there been an accident?

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:41.599
She and Daniel followed the sound, looking
for the source.

00:08:41.599 --> 00:08:43.320
"Are you guys okay?"

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.320
Daniel shouted.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.110
The lack of response spoke volumes.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.839
Whatever had happened, the rest of the group
was in big trouble.

00:08:49.839 --> 00:08:53.019
Bev quietly kicked herself for neglecting
to bring a first aid kit.

00:08:53.019 --> 00:08:56.550
Finally, the two reached the other end of
the mall, where the scream had sounded like

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:57.649
it was coming from.

00:08:57.649 --> 00:08:59.079
But there was no one there.

00:08:59.079 --> 00:09:01.990
Only a dark, wet smear along the ground.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:06.670
It looked incredibly fresh, and it smelled
metallic, violent.

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.270
Bev didn't have to look more closely to tell
that it was blood.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:14.650
Whatever had happened to the other three...she
wasn't sure they were going to find them alive.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.670
Daniel reached into his jacket pocket and
pulled out a small pocket knife.

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.930
"It's not much, but... just in case."

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:23.570
He held it out in front of them as they walked,
following the trail of blood.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:27.170
Something crashed to the ground behind them,
and Bev whirled around to see a large steel

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.320
beam only feet away.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:31.110
Any closer, and they would have been crushed.

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:36.019
Her eyes darted around, searching for any
more potential danger, and then...she saw

00:09:36.019 --> 00:09:37.019
it.

00:09:37.019 --> 00:09:39.510
Up in the rafters, by the ceiling, was a strange
figure.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:42.180
It was unlike anything she had ever seen.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:46.420
It was tall, impossibly tall, and pitch black.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:50.100
Its head was bulbous, with a pair of feline
ears on top.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:55.140
She could make out a nose, a pair of wide
white eyes with big dark pupils, and it was

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.140
smiling.

00:09:56.140 --> 00:10:00.089
A broad, wicked smile, filled with jagged
blood-stained teeth.

00:10:00.089 --> 00:10:02.470
Its hands looked like enormous white gloves.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:07.850
It was almost like...she felt ridiculous thinking
this even as terror prickled at the back of

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:12.050
her neck, but it looked like an old cartoon,
the sort of thing her grandmother used to

00:10:12.050 --> 00:10:13.050
watch.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:17.170
Except that those always looked friendly,
even if they were a little unsettling.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.870
This thing...it looked evil.

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:23.890
At first, she thought it was some sort of
twisted graffiti or a statue left by a macabre

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.260
experimental artist.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.750
But then, it moved.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:32.700
The creature tilted its head to the side,
its smile broadening and its pupils dilated.

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:36.910
It was looking right at her, and it was excited.

00:10:36.910 --> 00:10:37.910
"Daniel..."

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:38.950
Bev whispered weakly.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.100
"I see it too."

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.800
He replied, his voice shaking.

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.019
"We need to go.

00:10:43.019 --> 00:10:44.170
We need to go now."

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:47.680
Bev couldn't be sure what the thing would
do if it caught them, but she didn't want

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:49.570
to wait around to find out.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:52.000
She grabbed Daniel's arm, and yanked him toward
the exit.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:57.240
It took him a moment to start moving again,
paralyzed by fear and confusion at the incomprehensible

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.750
sight of the entity on the ceiling, but once
he started running, it seemed like he would

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:02.880
never stop.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:07.160
The two raced toward the exit, arms and legs
pumping as fast as they could.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.720
Behind them, they could hear the creature
chasing after them, but they didn't dare look

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:12.279
back to see.

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:16.150
Just before they passed the threshold out
of the mall, Bev felt Daniel's hand slip out

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.150
of hers.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:22.139
She spun around, searching for him, and watched
in helpless terror as the long, long arms

00:11:22.139 --> 00:11:27.050
of the creature looped around his chest, pulling
him back away from her and lifting him up

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.100
in the air.

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:33.730
It opened its massive mouth, wider, wider,
wider, and swallowed him whole.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:39.010
Bev screamed, but she forced herself to keep
running, to save herself from the same fate.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:43.560
She could feel the entity's eyes on her back
as she ran out the door, but once she escaped,

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:45.850
she knew it would not chase her any further.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.550
For some reason...it was letting her go.

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:53.139
She couldn't imagine it was out of some kind
of mercy, but she was grateful to escape with

00:11:53.139 --> 00:11:55.190
her life just the same.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:59.750
Bev stumbled into the local police station
a disheveled mess, face streaked with tears,

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:02.600
and told the officer on duty what she had
seen.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:07.390
He didn't believe her at first, asking her
to repeat her story again and again.

00:12:07.390 --> 00:12:10.850
Every time, she insisted that she knew what
she encountered out there.

00:12:10.850 --> 00:12:13.990
Or, at least, she knew that she couldn't explain
it.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:18.890
The officer sat her in an interrogation room
alone with a cup of coffee, and asked her

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:22.560
to wait until someone more qualified to help
her arrived.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:26.110
She wondered if they were going to try and
have her committed, if they had assumed she

00:12:26.110 --> 00:12:27.460
had lost her mind.

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:31.790
But when a man in a white lab coat opened
the door and greeted her, he said that he

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:32.860
believed her.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:36.000
He wasn't from a hospital, or affiliated with
the police.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:42.090
He was from a special organization, a Foundation
dedicated to investigating the unexplained.

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:45.140
He was going to look into what happened at
the mall.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:49.940
All he asked was that she tell him, in her
own words, what she had seen.

00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.220
"I don't know."

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.220
She sighed.

00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:55.589
"It looked like...some kind of messed up cartoon
cat."

00:12:55.589 --> 00:12:59.440
With the first-hand account of Bev, and a
series of confirmed disappearances that could

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:05.430
all be traced to the abandoned mall, the SCP
Foundation opened an official investigation.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.970
Wanting to eliminate as many potential complications
as possible, the Foundation selected only

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:14.430
one researcher actually enter the abandoned
building, an operative with a great deal of

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.130
field work experience named Dr. Baughan.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:21.380
Though Dr. Baughan would be entering the building
alone, he would not be without support.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:26.139
He would be fitted with a microphone and camera,
and his progress would be monitored remotely

00:13:26.139 --> 00:13:29.460
by a supervisor at a nearby Foundation site.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:33.899
If the need for backup arose, they would then
be able to deploy additional security officers

00:13:33.899 --> 00:13:37.440
to enter the mall and extract Dr. Baughan
if at all possible.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:42.790
He would also be armed, with a standard pistol
as well as a Foundation-issued flamethrower.

00:13:42.790 --> 00:13:47.130
With the team selected, and the appropriate
safety measures taken, it was time for Dr.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:51.839
Baughan to enter the mall and see just what
he could learn about the entity dwelling inside.

00:13:51.839 --> 00:13:57.500
If at all possible, he was to neutralize it
and bring it into containment alive so that

00:13:57.500 --> 00:14:00.600
it could be studied closely in a clinical
environment.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:05.209
If live capture was impossible, he was instructed
to terminate the being and bring its body

00:14:05.209 --> 00:14:07.610
in for a thorough autopsy.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.209
With his weapon already drawn and ready, and
his eyes sharp and alert, Dr. Baughan walked

00:14:12.209 --> 00:14:13.709
into the empty mall.

00:14:13.709 --> 00:14:18.440
He saw a lot of what Bev and her friends had
seen: the old pretzel stand, the dried-up

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:22.730
fountain, the creepy but harmless rows of
faceless mannequins still locked in the same

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:24.959
poses they had held for a decade.

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:29.699
The spiderwebs made him a little nervous,
but that was garden-variety arachnophobia

00:14:29.699 --> 00:14:31.829
more than any sense of real danger.

00:14:31.829 --> 00:14:34.070
"I don't know about this one, honestly."

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:37.269
He spoke into his microphone to his supervisor
on the other end.

00:14:37.269 --> 00:14:41.770
"So far, seems like this place is your standard
abandoned building death trap, maybe our missing

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:45.990
persons just weren't careful or properly trained
to deal with navigating a place like this."

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:47.250
"Just keep looking."

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.470
His supervisor ordered.

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:50.690
"Look for anything anomalous."

00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:51.690
"Got it."

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:52.860
Dr. Baughan nodded.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.880
He stepped on something with a loud CRUNCH.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:59.040
He looked down to see the oldest, stalest
soft pretzel he had ever seen.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.269
"Anyone hungry?"

00:15:00.269 --> 00:15:03.540
He quipped, turning his camera toward the
unappetizing sight.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:04.980
"Don't worry, I'll keep looking."

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:10.029
He carried on walking, heading past a shoe
store, a music store, some kind of novelty

00:15:10.029 --> 00:15:11.949
porcelain figurine store.

00:15:11.949 --> 00:15:15.209
He stopped at the toy store when something
eerie caught his eye.

00:15:15.209 --> 00:15:17.070
"You guys seeing this?"

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:18.070
He asked.

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:19.070
"What is it, Baughan?"

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:20.070
His supervisor replied.

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:22.709
"Just this creepy stuffed animal thing.

00:15:22.709 --> 00:15:24.240
The cat, right over there.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:27.050
I don't like how its eyes follow me when I
walk by."

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:28.620
"I don't see a cat."

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:33.560
Sure enough, when Dr. Baughan did a double-take,
the strange cat-like toy was nowhere to be

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:34.560
seen.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:36.990
"Well, there's your first anomalous activity..."

00:15:36.990 --> 00:15:40.029
He joked, though his heart was beginning to
pound nervously in his chest.

00:15:40.029 --> 00:15:41.110
"Keep looking."

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:44.029
He nodded, and continued his patrol of the
area.

00:15:44.029 --> 00:15:47.860
He couldn't get the face of that thing that
wasn't a toy out of his head.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:52.200
Its eyes, like the old Felix the Cat clock
his grandparents had in their guest room.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.699
That thing had scared the hell out of him
as a kid, he could never sleep in the room

00:15:55.699 --> 00:15:56.699
with it.

00:15:56.699 --> 00:16:01.620
All he could think about were its eyes going
back and forth, back and forth.

00:16:01.620 --> 00:16:03.120
He stopped in his tracks.

00:16:03.120 --> 00:16:07.959
He thought he could hear the sound of a ticking
clock, clear as day, just behind him.

00:16:07.959 --> 00:16:10.829
He turned to look, but there was no clock.

00:16:10.829 --> 00:16:15.339
Nothing but darkness and emptiness, the same
as everywhere else.

00:16:15.339 --> 00:16:17.639
He felt something suddenly tugging at his
foot.

00:16:17.639 --> 00:16:23.149
He looked, expecting to see an animal pulling
at his shoelace, something ordinary, but instead...He

00:16:23.149 --> 00:16:26.639
saw long, pointed fingers curling around his
ankle.

00:16:26.639 --> 00:16:31.540
He couldn't see what the fingers belonged
to, couldn't see a body, could only see a

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:35.990
long, looping snake of a shadowy arm curling
around the corner up ahead.

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:40.069
Before he could tell his supervisor what was
happening, the hand had grabbed hold of him

00:16:40.069 --> 00:16:42.230
and was dragging him across the ground.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:45.470
The hand lifted him off the floor, then dropped
him back down.

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:46.930
He felt the lens of his camera break.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:47.930
"Are you ok?

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:48.930
We lost visuals."

00:16:48.930 --> 00:16:49.930
"No!

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:50.930
No, I'm not!"

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:53.870
He shouted, as he looked up into the face
of pure evil.

00:16:53.870 --> 00:16:58.649
Its pupils were dark and endless, its eyes
bloodshot, its teeth bared.

00:16:58.649 --> 00:17:02.680
"Don't send in backup, repeat, do NOT send
in backup!

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.610
Oh god, oh god-"

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:07.819
The audio cut to static, and the signal was
lost.

00:17:07.819 --> 00:17:10.360
Dr. Baughan's body was never found.

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:14.419
The entity referred to as Cartoon Cat was
given the object class Keter, regarded as

00:17:14.419 --> 00:17:18.959
highly dangerous and nearly impossible to
contain due to its reality-bending nature.

00:17:18.959 --> 00:17:23.390
Because it cannot be physically contained,
the Foundation's solution to minimize Cartoon

00:17:23.390 --> 00:17:26.730
Cat's damage was to block off access to the
abandoned mall.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.810
All civilians were warned of a deadly amount
of radiation in the area, in order to deter

00:17:30.810 --> 00:17:36.910
them from conducting any more urban exploration,
vandalism, or other visits to the location.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:40.720
Any of the few survivors that have encountered
Cartoon Cat are given amnestics, and their

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:44.929
experiences are written off as substance-related
or vivid nightmares.

00:17:44.929 --> 00:17:48.840
The empty mall may not be the only place Cartoon
Cat has made its own.

00:17:48.840 --> 00:17:53.990
Nor is it likely to be the only building of
its kind that houses an anomalous monster.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:59.789
After all, when humanity decides to vacate
a place, to leave it standing vacant and abandoned,

00:17:59.789 --> 00:18:02.770
you never know what might decide to move in.

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:09.549
Now go check out “SCP-096 VS Siren Head”
and “SCP-4158 - Big Charlie” for more

00:18:09.549 --> 00:18:12.049
things made by the inimitable Trevor Henderson!

